    "text": "ArcBlog\n▾\nContent\nDashboard\nStudio\nPages\nWrite\nSite\nHeroes\nCategories\nTags\nSEO\nFeeds\nAppearance\nOperations\nOperations\nHub console\nMedia\nAgents\nEconomy\nOrders\nPolicy\nAccess\nSettlements & ledger\nFactory\nSettings\nGeneral\nDiagnostics\nArcBlog\nAbout\nRSS\n© 2026 ArcBlog\nDashboard\nNode identity, roles, taxonomy and recent activity for this ArcBlog instance.\nArcBlog\ndid:bloc…rcblog\nv0.3.7\n●\nok\nRoles\nbasic\nCapabilities\nblog.read,blog.write,blog.publish\nValues come from node/profile.json and node/health.json.\nIf a value above is empty, run: node scripts/arcblog-node.mjs init\nNetwork overview\nStudio side: how many Hubs this node has registered and how fresh they are. The per-Hub rows (sync state, freshness, last error) live on Hub, one click away.\nHubs registered\n5\nHubs fresh\n1\nHubs offline\n4\nNode DID\ndid:blocklet:arcblog\nEndpoint\n—\nRoles\nbasic\nTransport\nafs,mcp\nA dash (—) means the record does not carry the value, the record was never published, or this binding has not resolved yet — a cold first load does not resolve propBind (BUG-036/062, docs/arc-contracts.md §28.1); switching pages or reloading fills the values in. Nothing is rendered as 0 and no green light is invented.\nSource: node/health.json (hubs aggregate) + node/discovery.json (DID / endpoint / transport), both guest-readable and read verbatim.\nAnomaly alerts\nOne click to the page that owns the anomaly. This bar counts nothing: the platform's expression language has no length or comparison primitive (docs/arc-contracts.md §21), so a number here would have to be invented.\nHub sync\nSettlement / ledger\nAgent grants\nThe only pre-computed aggregate this instance publishes is node/health.json.hubs (total / fresh / offline) — it is shown verbatim in the network card above. Per-source failure counts are not derivable on this page.\nRecent published\nHello ArcBlog\ntechnology\n10 days ago\npaid-test-1790472790603\ntechnology\n1 day ago\nsign-test